var e=[`Zhang Xun`,`Yin Ziqi`],t=[{title:`A Row of Identical Men`,text:`Across the field stood a row of men, all dressed exactly alike.`,narration:`During the An Lushan rebellion in the Tang dynasty, Zhang Xun was holding a city. The enemy drew up their ranks outside, every coat of armour exactly the same, and there was no telling who was giving the orders — without finding that one man, you would not know where to push.`},{title:`One Reed Arrow`,text:`One reed arrow flew over, and the man who turned to shout orders — that was him.`,narration:`Zhang Xun had arrows cut from reeds. A reed arrow cannot hurt anyone: it does not even sting. The man it hit did not care at all, but the people around him turned to look — and the one who turned and shouted orders was the leader, Yin Ziqi.`}],n={question:`How do you find the leader among a row of men who all look exactly the same?`,options:[{text:`Shoot one harmless reed arrow and watch who reacts most`,hint:``},{text:`Drag them over one by one and ask`,hint:`Seize one and the rest scatter — you never get to the right man.`},{text:`Just guess one of them`,hint:`Guess wrong and the shot is wasted; you have to start over.`}],reveal:`Find the one who matters most — take him, and the whole row falls apart.`},r=[`With so many people, you can only catch them one by one`,`Taking the ringleader means knocking him down`],i=[{question:`What did Zhang Xun shoot across to test them?`,options:[`A harmless reed arrow`,`A sharp, quick knife`,`A big, hard piece of stone`],answer:0,explanation:`The arrow was cut from reeds, so it could not hurt anyone — what he wanted was not to wound, but to see who reacted the most.`},{question:`A crowd of classmates is making a noise on the playground. Who do you look at first?`,options:[`Whoever makes everyone go quiet by speaking`,`Whoever shouts the loudest of all the people there`,`Whoever runs the fastest on the playground`],answer:0,explanation:`The one everyone listens to is the leader of that crowd — finding him works far faster than shouting at each person in turn.`},{question:`During a big classroom clean-up everyone is milling about. What do you do first to share the work out quickly?`,options:[`Just listen to whoever shouts the loudest of them all`,`Everyone works alone without talking`,`Ask the best organizer to share out the jobs`],explanation:`Find the one who can organize best, and the whole crowd starts working together.`}],a={stages:[{levelScript:{hint:`Try a reed dart on each`}}]},o={figures:e,story:t,keyMoment:n,misconceptions:r,quiz:i,game:a};export{o as default,e as figures,a as game,n as keyMoment,r as misconceptions,i as quiz,t as story};